1
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:03,900
I had an interview today, too.

2
00:00:03,900 --> 00:00:05,300
I had a great interview

3
00:00:05,300 --> 00:00:08,000
with Admissions at Columbia University.

4
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:08,700
Really?

5
00:00:08,700 --> 00:00:10,100
What did they say?

6
00:00:10,100 --> 00:00:11,600
Will you get into the school?

7
00:00:11,600 --> 00:00:13,300
Well, they didn't say anything for sure.

8
00:00:13,300 --> 00:00:17,238
But I figure that with my grades and with my personality,

9
00:00:17,238 --> 00:00:19,100
I'll have no problem.

10
00:00:19,100 --> 00:00:21,400
Columbia's a terrific school.

11
00:00:21,400 --> 00:00:22,400
What are you going to do?

12
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:24,600
Do? I don't know.

13
00:00:24,600 --> 00:00:27,800
I also applied to NYU.

14
00:00:27,800 --> 00:00:29,200
You sound excited about Columbia.

15
00:00:29,200 --> 00:00:32,000
What's your problem, Mike?

16
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:34,086
Indecision. Indecision.

17
00:00:34,086 --> 00:00:34,900
It's not easy,

18
00:00:34,900 --> 00:00:37,152
and this is an important decision we have to make.

19
00:00:37,152 --> 00:00:38,200
What about you?

20
00:00:38,200 --> 00:00:40,400
How was your interview with Michigan?

21
00:00:40,400 --> 00:00:41,700
The interview was fine.

22
00:00:41,700 --> 00:00:43,641
It's a great college.

23
00:00:43,641 --> 00:00:44,600
It is.

24
00:00:44,600 --> 00:00:46,300
My father would like me to go there.

25
00:00:46,300 --> 00:00:48,800
He and my Grandpa both went there.

26
00:00:48,800 --> 00:00:50,500
Great medical school, too.

27
00:00:50,500 --> 00:00:52,700
I know.

28
00:00:52,700 --> 00:00:55,100
You can follow in your father's footsteps.

29
00:00:55,100 --> 00:00:59,100
Ah! I'd like to follow in my own footsteps, Mike.

30
00:00:59,100 --> 00:01:00,480
What do you want to study?

31
00:01:00,480 --> 00:01:02,139
I've been thinking.

32
00:01:02,139 --> 00:01:04,389
I think I want to study journalism

33
00:01:04,389 --> 00:01:06,611
to be a reporter--a newspaperman.

34
00:01:06,611 --> 00:01:09,802
You do a pretty good job on the Riverdale High School paper.

35
00:01:09,802 --> 00:01:12,198
And I've been thinking about it a lot lately.

36
00:01:12,198 --> 00:01:13,900
Have you discussed it with your parents?

37
00:01:13,900 --> 00:01:16,700
No. But I have to.

38
00:01:16,700 --> 00:01:28,591
OK. Let's talk.

39
00:01:28,591 --> 00:01:33,400
Hi, Son. Is everything all right?

40
00:01:33,400 --> 00:01:35,800
Hi, Dad. Everything's fine.

41
00:01:35,800 --> 00:01:37,500
I was just waiting for you to get home

42
00:01:37,500 --> 00:01:39,000
so we could talk.

43
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:41,400
Anything special you want to talk about?

44
00:01:41,400 --> 00:01:44,062
There is, Dad.

45
00:01:44,062 --> 00:01:45,800
I'm listening.

46
00:01:45,800 --> 00:01:50,100
Well, I know you and Mom have given up a lot

47
00:01:50,100 --> 00:01:53,300
to save money for my college tuition.

48
00:01:53,300 --> 00:01:55,300
We want you to go to college, Robbie.

49
00:01:55,300 --> 00:01:57,600
I know. I do.

50
00:01:57,600 --> 00:01:59,400
But?

51
00:01:59,400 --> 00:02:04,000
Well, I've thought a lot about which college,

52
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:06,000
and one of them is Columbia.

53
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:10,600
Columbia? Why Columbia?

54
00:02:10,600 --> 00:02:15,100
First, they have an excellent School of Journalism.

55
00:02:15,100 --> 00:02:17,741
They do.

56
00:02:17,741 --> 00:02:22,100
And your friends are planning to go to Columbia?

57
00:02:22,100 --> 00:02:24,075
That's only part of it.

58
00:02:24,075 --> 00:02:27,600
It's complicated.

59
00:02:27,600 --> 00:02:29,604
I'll try to explain.

60
00:02:29,604 --> 00:02:33,100
Mike and I had a hamburger this afternoon, and we talked.

61
00:02:33,100 --> 00:02:35,000
Yes?

62
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:38,100
Well, we talked about a lot of things.

63
00:02:38,100 --> 00:02:38,955
He applied to Columbia,

64
00:02:38,955 --> 00:02:41,100
and his interview was very successful.

65
00:02:41,100 --> 00:02:42,400
He thinks he'll be accepted,

66
00:02:42,400 --> 00:02:45,700
and he really wants to go there.

67
00:02:45,700 --> 00:02:49,400
Dean Rafer called me today.

68
00:02:49,400 --> 00:02:52,600
He told me he was very impressed with you.

69
00:02:52,600 --> 00:02:54,000
He's a nice man.

70
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:56,700
He was very kind.

71
00:02:56,700 --> 00:02:58,000
He told me

72
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:02,500
you had some doubts about wanting to go to Michigan.

73
00:03:02,500 --> 00:03:04,400
Yes. I do.

74
00:03:04,400 --> 00:03:08,600
I'm just not sure about what I want to do.

75
00:03:08,600 --> 00:03:11,314
That's OK.

76
00:03:11,314 --> 00:03:13,487
You understand?

77
00:03:13,487 --> 00:03:16,300
Let me tell you something, Robbie.

78
00:03:16,300 --> 00:03:22,702
Something that might be surprising to you.

79
00:03:22,702 --> 00:03:27,400
What? Tell me.

80
00:03:27,400 --> 00:03:33,800
Well, Grandpa wanted me to study engineering, like him.

81
00:03:33,800 --> 00:03:36,873
Well, I wasn't clear about my future,

82
00:03:36,873 --> 00:03:43,101
but I knew engineering was not for me.

83
00:03:43,101 --> 00:03:46,800
What did you tell Grandpa?

84
00:03:46,800 --> 00:03:49,800
The truth.

85
00:03:49,800 --> 00:03:51,171
Then you're not upset

86
00:03:51,171 --> 00:03:55,119
about my not wanting to go into medicine?

87
00:03:55,119 --> 00:03:57,300
I'm not upset at all.

88
00:03:57,300 --> 00:04:01,300
I'm just happy that we're able to talk about it.

89
00:04:01,300 --> 00:04:04,800
I am too, Dad.

90
00:04:04,800 --> 00:04:08,500
I suppose you want to apply to Columbia.

91
00:04:08,500 --> 00:04:15,023
Yes, but I also want to apply to several other colleges.

92
00:04:15,023 --> 00:04:16,500
I thought you wanted to go to Columbia.

93
00:04:16,500 --> 00:04:19,029
Well, I might want to go to Columbia.

94
00:04:19,029 --> 00:04:21,309
But I might not.

95
00:04:21,309 --> 00:04:25,480
I just want to be able to make my own decision.

96
00:04:25,480 --> 00:04:28,600
You're a real Stewart!

97
00:04:28,600 --> 00:04:32,700
And if I think about it long enough, you never know ...

98
00:04:32,700 --> 00:04:34,000
Never know what?

99
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:37,400
If I make my own decision,

100
00:04:37,400 --> 00:04:42,300
I might choose Michigan.

101
00:04:42,300 --> 00:04:44,900
Robbie, you're something!

102
00:04:44,900 --> 00:04:47,916
You know, when I was your age,

103
00:04:47,916 --> 00:04:50,916
I said exactly the same thing to Grandpa.
